Unravelling the complex Jenkins architecture 

Jenkins Master Node (Controller) - Orchestrates all workflows defined in the multi-step pipeline. For example; handling tasks such as scheduling a job, monitoring the jobs etc.

Jobs - collection of steps.

Jenkins Plugins - community developed modules that you can add to Jenkins Server. It is a kind of extension to Jenkins which provides more features that are otherwise not available in Jenkins by default.

Jenkins Credentials - With Jenkins pipelines, it can ask you to access a cloud account, a server, a database. Jenkins allows storing multiple types of secret keys as the credential. 

For example; 
Secret text
Username & password
SSH keys

Executors - Looks for agents to run the jobs.

Node - Jenkins agents are the working nodes. They are the ones that do all the Jenkins Job steps. These are dedicated machines or containers, which are used to perform build tasks.
